WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.960
- All right, y'all,
time for my first guest.

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:03.550
He's a country music legend,

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:05.570
he's had 10 number one albums,

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:09.170
and sold over 50 million
records all around the world.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:12.560
He's back now with his first
solo album in half a decade.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.280
It's called, "Here on Earth,"
you gotta check it out.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.290
Tim McGraw, get on in here!

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.200
Hey!

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.490
- Did I get it working?

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.350
- Yes, you did,
congratulations, well done.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.910
- I am so technically
unsavvy, it's unbelievable.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.110
- Oh my gosh, me too.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.440
I'm, this is not my forte whatsoever.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.273
How are you?

00:00:31.273 --> 00:00:32.760
How have y'all been in quarantine?

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.830
- Doing well, I mean, you know, it's,

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.900
I get bored pretty
quickly and pretty easily,

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.850
but other than that, it's been good.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.973
Watching a lot of movies, cooking a lot.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:44.240
We're lucky we have all
three of our daughters

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.073
are at home right now,

00:00:45.073 --> 00:00:47.160
so we've had had them
home for like a week.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.440
So it's good to spend
some time with those guys.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.580
And you know, it's been a
tough year for everybody.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.760
I mean, we've had two graduations
this year and you know,

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.750
they've been a little odd
and a little different,

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:56.927
but you know, you're trying to make

00:00:56.927 --> 00:00:57.993
the best out of everything.

00:00:57.993 --> 00:00:59.940
- It kind of stinks too,
though, when you're a graduate.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.380
'Cause I know one I graduated college

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.010
and one graduated high school, right?

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.400
- Yes, one graduated, our
youngest graduated high school

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.890
then our middle girl
graduated college, yes.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:09.070
- Yeah, that's kind of a bummer,

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.070
you worked so hard,
especially the college kid.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.600
And then you're like, okay, cool.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.220
Like, no celebration. (laughs)

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.510
- None at all, for sure.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.550
I mean, we had some like social distancing

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.210
and some Zoom kind of thing celebrations,

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:21.680
and here at the house, we had an outdoor,

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:24.290
with just our immediate family, you know,

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:26.620
our kids and my sister and her kids.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.410
So, and everybody's been tested.

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.570
And so we did the whole,
we did it all right,

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:31.820
but we stayed away from each other,

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.540
and sort of said hi across
the yard to each other.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:35.950
- Oh, that's really, that's good,

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.030
though I feel like everybody
has their little pod,

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:38.863
you know?
- Yeah.

00:01:38.863 --> 00:01:40.490
- That everybody, you
don't go outside of it,

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:42.455
then you all should be good.

00:01:42.455 --> 00:01:43.288
- For sure.

00:01:43.288 --> 00:01:45.150
- Well, I hear that Faith put
you to work in the garden.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:46.210
Are you cooking?

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.170
Are you cooking with the
stuff you're growing?

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:51.080
- No, no, I was doing some
flowers for her because-

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.170
- Oh, flowers!

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.490
- Yeah, because two of our
girls were driving home,

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:57.040
you know, nobody's flying, really,

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.520
so they were driving in from California

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.300
to just to be home for a little while.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.575
And so, Faith wanted me
to redo the front door

00:02:05.575 --> 00:02:07.690
and all of that and did
flowers all around the place.

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.210
So I spent a couple of
days doing some gardening,

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:12.027
trying to make it look nice
for when the kids get here.

00:02:12.027 --> 00:02:13.810
- Are you that guy that
kinda gets out there

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.213
and you can do that pretty easily?

00:02:15.213 --> 00:02:18.380
- I mean, I, if I have
all the equipment there

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:20.710
and all the stuff picked
out and I'm told what to do,

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:21.543
then I can do it.

00:02:21.543 --> 00:02:23.630
But if I have to come up
with too much on my own

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:24.470
then I'm not very good.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:25.980
But I just, when I was in high school,

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:29.730
my mom's pretty, pretty
artistic and has a green thumb

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.070
and always worked with plants and stuff.

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:32.360
So when I was in high school,

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.360
I spent a lot of time
working at a plant nursery,

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.960
mostly just hauling stuff, you know,

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:39.104
but I spent a lot of time
doing some yard work,

00:02:39.104 --> 00:02:42.117
and you know, that kind of thing.

00:02:42.117 --> 00:02:43.150
- I feel like foliage,

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:45.080
I feel like it can just
change the landscape

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:46.520
in such a beautiful way and like make it

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.740
so pretty and calming.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:50.550
And it's, I'm the same way.
- Yeah.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.300
- So, which daughter is this, though?

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.487
Singing with the dog?

00:02:54.487 --> 00:02:58.719
(singing)
(howling)

00:02:58.719 --> 00:03:00.969
(laughing)

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.260
Oh my God, that's so cute.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:08.710
Which daughter is that?

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:11.070
- That's Maggie, that's
the middle daughter.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:14.260
Yeah, and Stromboli's
the dog's name, yeah.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.250
- Very Italian, I like it.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:19.670
- Yeah, well, he's just,
he's a glorified bird dog's

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.627
all he is, but he's Italian.

00:03:21.627 --> 00:03:23.140
I think it's called an Italian Brocco.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.320
So we had a family of those dogs

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.520
and he's the last one left.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.283
Well, we have one more at the farm,

00:03:28.283 --> 00:03:31.220
but so we named 'em all Italian names.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.840
- I love that y'all are both singers

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.220
and even your dogs sing.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:35.413
That's awesome.

00:03:35.413 --> 00:03:36.246
(laughing)
It's like,

00:03:36.246 --> 00:03:37.570
it really is in the family.

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:39.430
- To be fair, Stromboli
sings a lot better than me,

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:41.070
I'm probably the worst
singer in the house.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.670
- Oh, shut up, I've seen you live,

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:44.760
you, that's that's what
I found so funny though,

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.130
I've seen you live, you and Faith,

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:47.480
and you came backstage and you were like,

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.130
oh man, if I'd you were
here, I would've sang better,

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:51.650
I was like, you did an awesome
job, I was singing along.

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:53.340
I was like, y'all both killed it.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.520
Like, you're so humble, whatever.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.130
He has just released his
first album in five years,

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.030
it's called "Here on Earth."

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.330
So Tim, when did you
actually finish the album?

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.740
I hear you tinkered all the
way 'til the end, right?

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.843
- Yeah. I mean, look, as you know,

00:04:08.008 --> 00:04:10.810
are you ever really finished
with making a record?

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.913
I mean, you sort of put
it in a barrel, right?

00:04:12.913 --> 00:04:14.430
You know, 'cause you can always,

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:15.720
and then you go back a year later

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:16.553
and you hear something, just dang,

00:04:16.553 --> 00:04:17.510
I wish I would've fixed that,

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:18.910
or I wish I'd have did
that a little different.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:21.580
It's always, you're always,
art's always a work in progress,

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:22.413
you're never finished with it.

00:04:22.413 --> 00:04:23.840
But yeah, I've been working on it,

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:27.770
gosh, it's been, Faith and
I did our Soul to Soul Tour

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:32.470
a couple of years, we
our first duets album,

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:35.050
so this is the first
solo album in five years

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:35.960
that I've done.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.610
But I worked on it like the last part

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:41.227
of our Soul to Soul Tour's
when I started working on it.

00:04:41.227 --> 00:04:43.993
And I spent a lot of
time flying in and out

00:04:43.993 --> 00:04:47.520
from being on the road and
spending the night in the studio,

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.353
working on it.

00:04:48.353 --> 00:04:49.990
And yeah, we tweaked it and worked on it

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:53.690
and kept messing with sounds
and messing with mixes

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.190
up until the last minute until it just

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.540
finally had to be turned in.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:59.010
- Yeah, no, I'm, I'm the same way.

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:00.120
I think they're all, like for artists,

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:01.030
it's like your little babies.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.310
And then you go out on the
road and you tour with it,

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:05.070
like you said, and you get
out there and you're like,

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.420
oh, you start doing something live,

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:08.500
you're like, I wish I'd had
done that in the studio.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:10.300
But so this album is
called "Here on Earth"

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.620
and it's about the meaning of life.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.470
Which is awesome 'cause
I literally have an album

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:17.310
called "Meaning of Life,"
but has that changed?

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:19.050
Which I didn't find it, by the way,

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:22.400
but it has that changed for you this year?

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.260
Like, what life is?

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:26.170
I feel like all of us have
been put in this situation,

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:28.220
like, literally every human on the planet

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.850
has been put in this like
quarantine kind of pandemic mode.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.640
And there's just so many challenges

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.040
that we're being faced with right now.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.750
And also like bringing back family

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:38.810
to kind of those simple kind of forms

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:41.710
and us not being able to
be as busy, most of us.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:42.680
Like, is that, do you think that

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:44.160
kind of affected you with this?

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:45.210
- Yeah, for sure.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:50.210
Did you know, it all came
together, you know, post,

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:53.190
we were working on it,
the pre pandemic, I guess,

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:56.770
but a lot of the songs
started making more sense

00:05:57.823 --> 00:06:02.823
contextually, after the
pandemic started happening,

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:05.460
we were in the middle of mixing
and we remixed a few things

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.140
after it all happened
just because we thought

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:09.450
it just needed a different
emotional pull to it

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:11.190
because of the things that were going on.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:13.260
And what I wanted to do with
this record, from the beginning

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.420
what I started out doing was
just sort of wanted to create,

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:18.250
I didn't wanna do sort of a linear story

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:21.090
or anything like that, or do
any kind of concept album.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:24.770
But I did wanna sort of
lay out a tapestry of life

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:27.060
in a lot of ways and indeed have each song

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:29.720
sort of reflect these vignettes
that are part of your life.

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:32.840
And then as you go through
life, as you mature,

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:35.040
from times, the things
that you did as teenagers

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.030
to the things that you do,
you know, as an older adult.

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:39.220
There's even a song about losing your dog,

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:40.650
you know, on this album.

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:42.651
- But it's your song, I love it.

00:06:42.651 --> 00:06:43.820
- I know, so it's just, you know,

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:46.120
it's just about, it's about the things

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.050
that we go through in life.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:50.140
And certainly now is a very
reflective time in a lot of ways

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:51.850
because of what we're all going through

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:53.280
and what we're all dealing with.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:56.930
And there's, you know, certainly
people are going through

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.260
some terrible times with it,

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:01.200
but also I think there is
a reconnection with family

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:02.540
and a reconnecting with your kids

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:04.960
and a reconnection with being at home

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:07.500
and sort of learning more about each other

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:08.850
and paying more attention to each other

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:11.330
and being a little bit more
respectful of each other's space

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.080
because of the sort of the
world we're living in now.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.050
- Yeah. I mean, perspective is definitely,

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:17.823
I think, the word for 2020.

00:07:18.937 --> 00:07:20.560
You know, I mean, 2020, I mean,

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:21.870
it's been a tough year, obviously.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:22.703
We've been talking about it,

00:07:22.703 --> 00:07:24.810
but it's been a tough year
for country music too.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:27.270
We've lost a few legends.

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:29.310
One of those was actually Kenny Rogers.

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:31.040
I know that was an idol of yours, right?

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:33.190
- For sure, Kenny Rogers was a big guy,

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:35.390
well might, and such a nice guy.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:36.600
And I got to sing with him,

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.520
you know, which was really incredible.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:41.510
The funniest memory I
have with Kenny Rogers,

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:43.040
a couple of memories I
have with Kenny Rogers,

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:46.800
but he came to one of my shows and he was,

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:49.170
we sang "She Believes in Me" together.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:50.450
He came to one of the shows

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:52.310
and it was one of the Soul to Soul shows,

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:54.480
and we had our stage was in
the round and in the center,

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:55.857
and the only way to get out to the stage

00:07:55.857 --> 00:07:57.610
was to be in some sort of road case

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:00.500
or so we was tried to get Kenny Rogers out

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.400
to under the stage to
do this song with me.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:05.380
So he gets into a laundry hamper.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:08.670
So, imagine Kenny Rogers
getting into a laundry hamper

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:11.270
and laying down, and covering
him up and rolling him out

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:13.087
under the stage and him coming
up and just you leaves a bit,

00:08:13.087 --> 00:08:15.580
which was really a special moment for me.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:18.070
And then another Kenny
Rogers memory I have

00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:21.080
is he played the Monroe Civic Center

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:24.440
And my mom was a huge Kenny Rogers fan.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.370
And so, she took me out
of school that morning,

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:27.610
I think I was in the sixth grade,

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:28.890
seventh grade, or something like that.

00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:30.540
She took me out of school that morning.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:33.500
I got, put me in line at
the Monroe Civic Center

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.140
and I made it all the way to the window

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:38.248
before it sold out and I
didn't get to get tickets.

00:08:38.248 --> 00:08:39.081
(groans)

00:08:39.081 --> 00:08:41.260
But later on, I was in
college and I was working,

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:43.030
selling popcorn at the Monroe Civic Center

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:45.940
and I got to see a Kenny
Rogers concert selling popcorn.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:48.050
- Oh my gosh, that's so,
I have sold popcorn too,

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:49.170
at a movie theater.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.948
All our previous jobs.

00:08:50.948 --> 00:08:52.190
- Yes, for sure.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:53.220
- But wait, before we go,

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:57.460
I wanna ask about some rad
cowboy skills that I saw.

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:59.610
So, who taught you how to rope?

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:04.030
- Oh, well, (laughs) I grew up riding.

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:05.990
I could, I mean, my whole life was spent,

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:10.930
my stepdad was a cowboy and
spent a lot of time on horses.

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.310
God, that was funny.

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:14.850
I could ride and rope before
I could walk, practically.

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:15.730
So I spent a lot of time doing that

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:17.890
and now, I spent some time
in a high school rodeo

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:20.040
when I was a kid, rode
some bareback horses

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.907
and some team roping and some calf roping.

00:09:21.907 --> 00:09:24.560
So, I've done a little bit
of that my life, for sure.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.220
- It's so great to see you again, Tim,

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:28.680
please tell your lovely
family I say hello.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:30.710
And y'all be sure to
check out Tim's new album,

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:32.357
it's called "Here on Earth."

